</section>


  <div id="FAQ" class="pricing pt-5 pb-5 faq mb-5">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-lg-8 offset-lg-2 col-md-10 offset-md-1 text-center mt-4">
        <h4 class="title mt-0 mb-5">FAQs</h4>
        <div class="faq-block">
          <div class="question">How are searches counted?</div>
          <div class="answer"><p>Only successful searches are counted toward your monthly searches. Cached, errored, and failed searches are not. The number of results returned per response will not affect the number of credits used—responses with 100 results or empty result sets will both count as 1 search.</p>
</div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-block">
          <div class="question">Can we upgrade, downgrade, or cancel at any time?</div>
          <div class="answer"><p>Yes, you can upgrade, downgrade, or cancel your plan at any time without any restrictions.</p>
</div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-block">
          <div class="question">What happens if I cancel before my plan expires?</div>
          <div class="answer"><p>If you cancel before your plan expires, you can continue to use your remaining searches until the renewal date. After that, your plan will not be renewed.</p>
</div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-block">
          <div class="question">What happens when I upgrade my plan?</div>
          <div class="answer"><p>When you upgrade your plan, you'll only pay the difference between your current plan and the new one. Your renewal date will remain the same.</p>
</div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-block">
          <div class="question">What happens when I downgrade my plan?</div>
          <div class="answer"><p>When you downgrade your plan, you'll keep your current renewal date, and your subscription will renew at the lower plan rate. Any remaining searches from your previous plan will be added to your 'Extra Credits' balance.</p>
</div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-block">
          <div class="question">What happens if I run out of searches in a month?</div>
          <div class="answer"><p>You can set your plan to Automatic Early Renewal. It will trigger an early renewal once you've used all your searches. You can toggle the Automatic Early Renewal anytime by visiting <a href="https://serpapi.com/plan">this page</a>. You can also renew your plan manually. In both cases, your searches will be fully replenished, your renewal date will be updated, and your searches will reset at the start of the new billing cycle.</p>
</div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-block">
          <div class="question">What&#39;s your refund policy?</div>
          <div class="answer"><p>We offer a full refund within 7 days of the date you subscribed to a plan unless you've used more than 20% of your searches.</p>
</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <script type="text/javascript">
    $(document).on("click", ".faq-block .question", function(event){
      event.preventDefault();
      $(this).next('.answer').slideToggle(200);
    });
  </script>
  </div>
</main>

